  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>With respect to the compounds <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> choose the correct statement(s).</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/989d0f80-f764-4d35-be69-931fe66b2eb9-image.png\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "MaWTV",
      "text": "The acidity of compound&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is due to delocalization in the conjugate base.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bewFm",
      "text": "The conjugate base of compound&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math>&nbsp;is aromatic.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6SWhh",
      "text": "Compound&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;becomes more acidic, when it has a<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;substituent.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "v55hA",
      "text": "The acidity of compounds follows the order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>III</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/78e8ff59-dafa-4820-89a6-f57823d70ccc-image.png\"/> </p><p>is stabilised by conjugation</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> Conjugation base of  <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/0969b6cd-5a4a-49b7-b418-97930ccd18ae-image.png\"/> is <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/0d99b291-7c8d-4623-9b66-0fffeffa6f9f-image.png\"/> which is an aromatic anion</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>  group is an electron withdrawing group it increases acidic strength of any compound to which<br/>it is added.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>)</mo></math> The acidic strength order on the basis of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> data <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi><mo>></mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>></mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>></mo><mi>II</mi><mo>></mo><mi>III</mi></math> is </p>",
    "image": null
  },
